# wip251: the ARP page (step 1): ARP = the SEQ view with a piano for keys. SELECT chooses the voice, OCT- / OCT+ the keyboard octave
# (-3..+3), every key (white and black) plays the selected voice: key C (raw key 7) = its own pitch, key k = k - 7 semitones,
# the octave moves it by 12. Nothing is stored (the patterns stay as they are); SEQ goes back to the SEQ page.
wait 300
snapproj
expect arp 0
tap ARP
wait 50
expect view 7
expect arp 1
expect arpoct 0
expect sel 0
shot arp_page.png
# wip287: ALGO chooses the voice (SELECT is the SEQ page's: it no longer changes the voice)
turn ALGO 1
expect sel 1
turn ALGO 1
turn ALGO -1
turn ALGO -1
expect sel 0
turn ALGO -1
expect sel 7
turn ALGO 1
expect sel 0
turn SELECT 1
expect sel 0
expect acsel 0
tapkey 7
expect arpnote 0
tapkey 19
expect arpnote 12
tapkey 0
expect arpnote -7
tapkey 26
expect arpnote 19
tapkey b10
expect arpnote 18
tap OCT+
expect arpoct 1
shot arp_oct1.png
tapkey 7
expect arpnote 12
tapkey 0
expect arpnote 5
tap OCT+
tap OCT+
tap OCT+
expect arpoct 3
tapkey 7
expect arpnote 36
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
expect arpoct -3
tapkey 7
expect arpnote -36
# the keys are notes, not steps or FUNC: nothing in the project changed
expect projsame 1
# the ARP page again after another page; SEQ is the SEQ page
tap HOME
tap ARP
expect arp 1
tap SEQ
wait 50
expect arp 0
expect view 7
tap ARP
tap HOME
tap SEQ
expect arp 0
# on the SEQ page a white key is a step again (and SELECT does not change the voice)
expect sel 0
